  "distractor_1": "Negotiate UI capability at session start; hosts request ui:// when advertised, otherwise automatically retry later without text fallbacks.",
  "explanation_why_it_is_incorrect_1": "This relies on session-level capability negotiation and retries instead of always providing machine-readable text-only fallbacks; blocked or policy-restricted hosts may never render ui://, causing broken or partial tool execution.",
  "thinking_process_1": "Used the source quote requiring servers to provide text-only fallbacks. Crafted a plausible alternative focused on capability negotiation (a different technology/service approach) that might work elsewhere but fails here. Matched style to the correct answer and ensured the distractor text is 18 words to satisfy the length constraint."
}
